            <ArticleTitle>Facet syndrome: clinical signs, symptoms, diagnosis, and treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Low back pain is a major health problem in the United States today. Nearly 80% of Americans experience low back pain during their lifetime, with facet syndrome accounting for a large percentage of these symptoms. A recent study on low back pain showed involvement of one or more facet joints in 79% of the patients studied, while ruptured disc involvement was present in only 1%. This report investigates facet syndrome, its anatomy, etiology, clinical signs and symptoms, diagnosis, and various methods of treatment and patient management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
